WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--------------------

Session Echo is built from a private source repository and distributed as
public binaries. Nobody receiving a build can read its commit history, so the
history cannot serve as the record of where this software came from. This file
is that record. It is the attribution the MIT License requires, in the only
place a recipient of a binary can actually see it.


PROVENANCE
----------

Session Echo is a hard fork of the project now published as `anarlog`. There
are no ongoing merges from upstream.

The upstream history begins on 2024-12-09 and the project was renamed several
times before this fork was taken. Established from the repository history:

  2024-12-09  Fastnote
              Initial commit (31c9422cd). The README read "# Fastnote" and
              package.json declared "name": "fastnote".

  2025        Hyprnote
              In use by 2025-05-04 (#719, "Welcome to Hyprnote"); the README
              was rewritten for Hyprnote branding on 2025-11-16 (5c33b0a06),
              and application data directories and bundle identifiers were
              migrated to `hyprnote` in November 2025 (#1680, #1687).

  2026-02     Char
              Product renamed from Hyprnote to Char (#3998, #4247, and the
              content migration in #3937). Char was a product name only — no
              separate public repository under that name exists.

  2026-04/05  Anarlog
              Renamed again to Anarlog: README (#5131, 2026-04-26),
              application naming (#5286, 2026-05-20), and storage paths
              (#5314). Remaining `fastrepl/char` references were repointed at
              `fastrepl/anarlog` on 2026-08-12 (#6678).

  2026-08-27  Session Echo
              Forked and rebranded by Flagbit GmbH & Co. KG (3077c1a29,
              "rename to Session Echo with de.flagbit bundle identifiers").

Throughout that chain the repository was a single, continuously renamed
project. The upstream repository remains public at
https://github.com/fastrepl/anarlog, and the older URL
https://github.com/fastrepl/hyprnote redirects to it.

The names "Fastnote", "Hyprnote", "Char", "Anarlog" and "Fastrepl" are the
upstream project's and its authors' marks. They were removed from Session Echo
for trademark reasons, not licensing ones; the MIT License grants no rights in
them. Their use above is factual attribution of origin, not a claim to them.


WHAT WAS REMOVED FROM THE UPSTREAM PROJECT
------------------------------------------

Session Echo is a subtractive fork. Notably, the upstream `enterprise/` tree —
server-side meeting-bot infrastructure that was commercially licensed by
Fastrepl, Inc. and not covered by the MIT License — was deleted in full, along
with its separate license files. No commercially licensed upstream code is
present in Session Echo, and none is distributed with its binaries.

The hosted API, the web application and the mobile applications were removed as
well.


